# Operation Authority v1

**Status:** Complete · Closed · Foundational Authority

**Mission:** Own Operation Class. Nothing else.

## Owns

- Operation
- Operation Class

## Does not own

Service definitions · Standard labor · Inspection templates · Parts · Advisor workflow · Pricing · Technician workflow · Catalog management · Search · UI · **shop default labor category** (Labor Categories owns that)

Seeded `operations` rows are temporary records so Pricing can resolve Operation Class — **not a service catalog**. Expand only when another capability earns it.

## Consumer

Estimate Pricing Engine (consumes Operation Class only).

## Contract

```text
Estimate Line → Operation → owns Operation Class → Estimate Pricing Engine
```

## Permanent invariants

1. Operation owns Operation Class.
2. Pricing never infers Operation Class.
3. Pricing consumes Operation Class only (`$operation->operationClassKey()` / relation).
4. Operation Authority never prices labor.
5. Estimate Pricing never owns Operation metadata.

## One question

`$operation->operationClassKey()` — the record is the authority. No OperationResolver.

## Authority richness

**Authorities may begin life with a single field if that field is the operational truth they own.**

Richness comes from operational pressure — not imagination. A thin Operation that only owns `operation_class_id` is enough until the shop earns more.

## Migration follow-ups (approved; do not freeze as permanent)

1. Delete `Operation::forLine(..., code)` / shop-default category bridge once `operation_id` is universal on labor lines.
2. (Pricing consumer) Delete labor-category → posture inference once Billing Posture is always explicit on resolve.

These are **deletions** of transitional compatibility paths after operational adoption demonstrates they are unused — not future improvements.

`Operation::forShopDefaultLaborCategory()` is transitional loading only — not doctrine ownership of the default.

**Pre-production:** Count Billing Posture Resolution (`explicit` · `category_inference` · `default`) so inference can be removed when the counter is zero.

## Reopen criteria

Verified defects only. Not metadata, pickers, or catalogs — those are other capabilities.
